Stored data checked directly: IDs 1–12 correspond, in order, to the variants above. ID 3 is exactly “Donations and other support (including loans) for activities as an MP”. Recent donations/support uses only that variant; gifts and visits retain their own categories. The overview is explicitly “Known recorded amounts across all declarations”, covering every category, not labelled a donations total. Unknown IDs remain visible with their source name, but are not silently classified as donations.

The repository retains its repeatable-read profile/declarations transaction, removes LIMIT, selects category_id, and preserves the left joins and e.id ordering. Stable order remains registration DESC NULLS LAST, source ID DESC, entry ID. Count comes from the resulting complete declarations, removing a redundant count query and window metadata. No migration is necessary; SQL uses sqlx macros and refreshed offline metadata.

Summary uses a BTreeMap keyed by normalized currency, then source category ID and recorded source name. All occurrences contribute once, including duplicates and negative amounts. No occurrence is created for a left-joined empty declaration. Totals start None and become Some only after a known amount; exact zero is distinct from unknown. Currency trimming uses the existing CURRENCY_WHITESPACE constant in the member SQL projection as it does for funder aggregation; no copied Rust/JS currency normalization. Null/blank currency occurrences contribute to unknown_currency_count, never a fake currency total. Unknown-amount counts are retained per currency/category. Summary scans the complete dataset; recent_donations is category-filtered first and then takes five in repository order.

This is a deep member(id) interface: it owns completeness, scope, exact aggregation and recent-selection policy while callers choose a page. It exposes neither SQL windows nor aggregation stages. Boundary parsing stays in the repository and TS response parser; domain rules stay in the category enum and service.

## Module plan

- `domain/models/declaration.rs`: category identity and classification; no mirrored ID lists in SQL, handlers or TS.
- `domain/models/entity_details.rs`: rename RecentDeclaration, add member summary records, remove bounded-member metadata.
- `domain/repositories/entity_details.rs`, `outbound/entity_details.rs`: one complete consistent MemberRecord read; existing funder path retained.
- `domain/services/entity_details.rs`: pure exact summary and recent donation selection; no second member service endpoint.
- `inbound/http/handlers/entity_details.rs`: decimal strings, numeric category_id plus category_name; serialize summary and history together. Canonical enum performs ID conversion.
- `frontend/src/lib/entity-details.ts`: parse new contract from unknown, reuse declaration reader, add member-history route kind/view and shared member endpoint loading. History length is its total count.
- `frontend/src/MemberSummary.svelte`, `MemberHistory.svelte`: focused views; `EntityDetails.svelte` retains shared load/error/profile behavior and delegates. `App.svelte` accepts the new route. Native links preserve q/strictness between summary, history and search.
- Registration bounds compare UTC YYYY-MM-DD inclusively. Null dates remain visible without bounds and are excluded with active bounds; explain this beside filters. Invalid/reversed bounds show a field error. Filter changes reset page; empty results remain distinct from an empty register.
- Currency sections show exact textual values and horizontal signed bars with a common zero baseline. Calculate relative widths from decimal coefficients using BigInt and an integer 0–10000 ratio; only bounded ratios become JS numbers. Scale by maximum absolute category amount, not signed net total. Unknown totals have no bar and an explicit unavailable label. Mobile stacks labels and wraps amounts.

## Tradeoffs accepted

We accept sending the full member dataset to the summary view in exchange for one consistent read contract and no duplicated aggregate SQL/category policy. A five-item recent subset duplicates a bounded amount of payload to keep selection policy entirely in the service. If measured payload becomes excessive, preserve the complete repository read and split DTO endpoints later; no speculative cache.

## Alternatives considered

Separate summary and full-history endpoints hide payload size but add two handlers, loaders and service paths, and either duplicate repository reads or introduce SQL classification/aggregation ownership. They are justified by measured size, not the current requirement. A frontend-only summary avoids Rust summary records but moves financial arithmetic and domain selection into JS and invites divergent rules; rejected.

